# Copy to .env and set for this machine. Not committed.
#
# RPE_DATA_ROOT is the pipeline tree holding Inputs/, Outputs/ and Build Artifacts/.
# It differs per machine and must never be hardcoded in the build code — see
# build/rpe_env.py. Repointing this line is the ONLY change a new machine needs.

# The pipeline runs LOCALLY and Drive is a write-only backup (Aaron, 2026-09-09).
# Nothing reads Drive. The backup direction is local -> Drive, never the reverse:
# a file copied back, or read from Drive by a build, recreates the two-stores
# problem that shipped month-old ICS figures in August. If the two ever differ,
# local wins.

# --- Windows — this machine, moved 2026-09-09 ---
RPE_DATA_ROOT=C:\Data Pipelines\RPE Pipeline

# --- Mac (Google Drive for Desktop), if a Mac ever runs this again ---
# RPE_DATA_ROOT=/Users/<you>/Library/CloudStorage/GoogleDrive-<account>/My Drive/Work/RPE Pipeline

# --- Superseded: G:\My Drive\Work\RPE Pipeline (2026-08-31 to 2026-09-09) ---
# Drive was the source for both inputs and outputs while Aaron worked out of it.
# It is now the backup target only. The tree that moved was 308 files / 1.23 GB,
# verified by file count, byte total and hash before .env was repointed.

# --- Note: C:\Data Pipelines\ also holds "Renewals Pipeline" ---
# A DIFFERENT project with its own Inputs\ and Outputs\, easy to mistake for this
# one at a glance. RPE is the sibling folder "RPE Pipeline". A wrong root fails
# loudly — rpe_env.data_root() raises on a path that is not a directory.

# --- The CSI source shares (unchanged by the move; both need the VPN) ---
# These are where the data team LANDS files; scripts/watch_sources.py copies from
# them into Inputs/. They are separate from RPE_DATA_ROOT and default to the paths
# in scripts/deck_status.py — set these only to override.
# RPE_SRC_ODDD=\\PADMIS105\Velocity_company\Aburgard\ODDD
# RPE_SRC_REPORTS=\\PADMIS105\Velocity_clientreports
